{
 "duration": 58.472,
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "n1",
   "text": "What if you never slept again?",
   "start": 0.35,
   "end": 2.366
  },
  {
   "id": "n2",
   "text": "Sleep eats about a third of your life. Twenty-six years, just lying there.",
   "start": 2.606,
   "end": 6.827
  },
  {
   "id": "n3",
   "text": "So let's delete it. Here's you, at hour zero.",
   "start": 7.067,
   "end": 10.117
  },
  {
   "id": "n4",
   "text": "By hour seventeen, your reactions are as slow as if you'd had a couple of drinks.",
   "start": 10.357,
   "end": 14.744
  },
  {
   "id": "n5",
   "text": "At twenty-four, you're driving like you're legally drunk.",
   "start": 14.984,
   "end": 18.111
  },
  {
   "id": "n6",
   "text": "Meanwhile, inside your head, the trash is piling up.",
   "start": 18.351,
   "end": 21.674
  },
  {
   "id": "n7",
   "text": "During sleep, your brain cells shrink apart, and fluid washes out waste, like proteins linked to Alzheimer's.",
   "start": 21.914,
   "end": 27.985
  },
  {
   "id": "n8",
   "text": "No sleep, no wash.",
   "start": 28.225,
   "end": 30.066
  },
  {
   "id": "n9",
   "text": "Day two. Your brain starts shutting off without asking. Microsleeps, a few seconds at a time, sometimes with your eyes open.",
   "start": 30.306,
   "end": 37.002
  },
  {
   "id": "n10",
   "text": "Day three. The walls start to breathe.",
   "start": 37.242,
   "end": 39.764
  },
  {
   "id": "n11",
   "text": "The record? In 1964, seventeen-year-old Randy Gardner stayed awake for eleven days straight.",
   "start": 40.004,
   "end": 45.708
  },
  {
   "id": "n12",
   "text": "Lab rats kept fully awake died within a few weeks.",
   "start": 45.948,
   "end": 49.318
  },
  {
   "id": "n13a",
   "text": "And Randy? He slept almost fifteen hours.",
   "start": 49.558,
   "end": 52.425
  },
  {
   "id": "n13b",
   "text": "And woke up fine.",
   "start": 52.785,
   "end": 54.307
  },
  {
   "id": "n14",
   "text": "So tonight, when your pillow calls, pick up.",
   "start": 54.547,
   "end": 57.272
  }
 ],
